Subject: [PATCH] Compile the realigner's fixed CIGAR regex once per worker (#1116)

The chr20 make_examples sample shows RE2 construction and compilation under
CigarStringToVector. The pattern never changes. Reuse it for each worker's
read/haplotype alignments, keeping exactly the same parsing and avoiding
shared matching-cache contention between workers.

diff --git a/deepvariant/realigner/fast_pass_aligner.cc b/deepvariant/realigner/fast_pass_aligner.cc
--- a/deepvariant/realigner/fast_pass_aligner.cc
+++ b/deepvariant/realigner/fast_pass_aligner.cc
@@ -346,7 +346,7 @@
 std::list<CigarOp> CigarStringToVector(absl::string_view cigar) {
   std::list<CigarOp> cigarOps;
   absl::string_view input(cigar);
-  RE2 pattern("(\\d+)([XIDS=])");
+  static thread_local const RE2 pattern("(\\d+)([XIDS=])");
   int opLen;
   string opType;
   while (RE2::Consume(&input, pattern, &opLen, &opType)) {
